<edge source="us_iran_confront::transit_disruption_rate" target="china_eu_tech_rivalry::ai_asset_price_volatilit" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Repeated maritime interdictions through key chokepoints create shortfalls and shipment delays for AI hardware (chips, racks), triggering sudden supply‑driven repricing and larger intraday swings in AI‑exposed equities and component suppliers.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confront</data>
  <data key="d40">china_eu_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_confront::transit_disruption_rate" target="japan_fx_bond_stress::cross_border_flows" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Repeated maritime disruptions force Japanese importers to draw on foreign credit lines and pre-finance shipments while exporters accelerate or delay receipts, producing immediate net cross-border capital movements (larger gross flows and temporary net inflows to cover trade financing needs).</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confront</data>
  <data key="d40">japan_fx_bond_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_confront::transit_disruption_rate" target="opec_energy_volatility::crude_oil_price" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">More frequent incidents raise freight and insurance costs, reduce available tanker capacity and force longer routings or cargo delays, which raise market risk premia and prompt near-term upward moves in benchmark crude prices even before full physical shortages appear.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confront</data>
  <data key="d40">opec_energy_volatility</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_confront::transit_disruption_rate" target="rus_ukr_war::energy_supply_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased disruptions to shipping through key chokepoints (e.g., tanker attacks, interdictions) force rerouting, delay deliveries and raise insurance/operational constraints that directly reduce timely crude and refined fuel shipments into European and Black Sea supply chains serving Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confront</data>
  <data key="d40">rus_ukr_war</data>
</edge>
