<edge source="us_iran_confront::crude_supply_gap" target="japan_fx_bond_stress::long_term_yield_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A physical shortfall in crude availability raises near-term energy procurement and hedging requirements, prompting larger sovereign issuance and a higher term premium as markets price increased fiscal and balance-of-payments funding needs, pushing long-term yields up.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confront</data>
  <data key="d40">japan_fx_bond_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_confront::crude_supply_gap" target="opec_energy_volatility::crude_oil_price" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">A measurable net shortfall in physical crude availability tightens the supply–demand balance and triggers inventory draws and speculative buying, producing an immediate and sustained upward effect on crude benchmark prices.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confront</data>
  <data key="d40">opec_energy_volatility</data>
</edge>
