<edge source="rus_ukr_war::cross_border_strike_rate" target="china_eu_tech_rivalry::regulatory_scrutiny" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">An uptick in cross‑border strikes that demonstrably employ drones, guidance systems or autonomy accelerates policymaker concern over weaponized AI and drives faster adoption of rules limiting procurement, deployment, and third‑party AI components.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">rus_ukr_war</data>
  <data key="d40">china_eu_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="rus_ukr_war::cross_border_strike_rate" target="japan_fx_bond_stress::investor_positioning" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising cross-border strike rates heighten acute geopolitical tail risk and prompt global investors to cut directional risk and leverage (e.g., unwind carry trades and long-duration positions), reducing aggregate investor positioning in Japan-linked FX and bond markets.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">rus_ukr_war</data>
  <data key="d40">japan_fx_bond_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="rus_ukr_war::cross_border_strike_rate" target="opec_energy_volatility::maritime_transit_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased missile, drone, and naval strikes that target or occur near ports, merchant vessels, and sea lanes raise the probability of ship damage, rerouting, insurance claims, and temporary closures, directly increasing transit risk for commercial shipping.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">rus_ukr_war</data>
  <data key="d40">opec_energy_volatility</data>
</edge>
<edge source="rus_ukr_war::cross_border_strike_rate" target="opec_energy_volatility::energy_supply_disruption" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher rates of cross‑border strikes that hit terminals, storage, pipelines, or power infrastructure cause direct outages, export shutdowns, or evacuation of facilities, producing immediate interruptions to oil and gas deliveries.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">rus_ukr_war</data>
  <data key="d40">opec_energy_volatility</data>
</edge>
<edge source="rus_ukr_war::cross_border_strike_rate" target="us_iran_confront::transit_disruption_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Intensified cross-border strikes against Black Sea ports and maritime infrastructure divert merchant traffic into alternative routes and draw NATO/U.S. naval assets toward Europe, reducing deterrent presence in the Gulf and creating openings for Iran or its proxies to increase interdictions and attacks on shipping.</data>
