<edge source="rus_ukr_war::energy_supply_flow" target="china_eu_tech_rivalry::ai_capital_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Reductions or interruptions in energy shipments to Europe raise operating costs and reliability risk for energy‑intensive AI datacenters and HPC clusters, prompting investors to delay or withdraw funding for regional AI projects.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">rus_ukr_war</data>
  <data key="d40">china_eu_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="rus_ukr_war::energy_supply_flow" target="japan_fx_bond_stress::policy_rate_expectations" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">An increase in energy supply flow reduces imported energy inflation for Japan, lowering market-implied expectations that the Bank of Japan will need to tighten policy in the near term.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">rus_ukr_war</data>
  <data key="d40">japan_fx_bond_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="rus_ukr_war::energy_supply_flow" target="opec_energy_volatility::crude_oil_price" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">Changes in physical flows of oil and refined products from the conflict region (pipelines, export terminals) alter global available supply and prompt near‑term price adjustments as markets rebalance and traders price in shortages or gluts.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">rus_ukr_war</data>
  <data key="d40">opec_energy_volatility</data>
</edge>
<edge source="rus_ukr_war::energy_supply_flow" target="us_iran_confront::oil_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">A reduction in Russian energy supply flows tightens global crude balances and raises benchmark prices, whereas an increase in those flows exerts downward pressure on the oil price level observed in the US–Iran confrontation context.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">rus_ukr_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_confront</data>
</edge>
