<edge source="opec_energy_volatility::energy_supply_disruption" target="china_eu_tech_rivalry::ai_capital_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Physical interruptions to oil and gas deliveries raise operational and electricity costs for data centres and cloud providers in China and the EU, increasing project economics and lead‑time risks and causing investors to defer or reduce AI funding.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">opec_energy_volatility</data>
  <data key="d40">china_eu_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="opec_energy_volatility::energy_supply_disruption" target="japan_fx_bond_stress::cross_border_flows" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Physical interruptions to oil and gas deliveries trigger commodity-price spikes and risk‑off reallocation, prompting net portfolio inflows into perceived safe‑haven Japanese assets (JPY and JGBs) and altering cross‑border capital flows into Japan.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">opec_energy_volatility</data>
  <data key="d40">japan_fx_bond_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="opec_energy_volatility::energy_supply_disruption" target="rus_ukr_war::economic_activity_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Interruptions to oil and gas deliveries create immediate fuel and feedstock shortages and spike local energy prices, curtailing industrial production, transport and commercial activity in the affected war‑zone economies.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">opec_energy_volatility</data>
  <data key="d40">rus_ukr_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="opec_energy_volatility::energy_supply_disruption" target="us_iran_confront::mil_escalation_threat" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Physical interruptions of oil and gas deliveries that are attributed to Iran or its proxies prompt the US to increase naval escorts, strikes on perceived perpetrators, and deterrent deployments, directly raising the threat of military escalation.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">opec_energy_volatility</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_confront</data>
