  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Acute JPY/ JGB stress prompts Japanese insurers, pension funds and funds to repatriate or liquidate foreign holdings, directly reducing new outbound venture, PE and portfolio capital that had been funding AI startups and infrastructure in China and the EU.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">japan_fx_bond_stress</data>
  <data key="d40">china_eu_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="japan_fx_bond_stress::cross_border_flows" target="rus_ukr_war::logistics_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Large net repatriation of capital out of Japan into safe assets drains dollar liquidity and correspondent-bank balances in key clearing networks, causing short-term shortages in trade finance and freight payment channels that directly constrain transport, transshipment and resupply throughput into the conflict theater.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">japan_fx_bond_stress</data>
  <data key="d40">rus_ukr_war</data>
